{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall overlay it with gold.</b> It would have been fitting for the ark to be entirely of gold, but it would be heavy to carry. Its law is to be carried on the shoulder, as it is written: 'for the service of the holy is upon them; on the shoulder they shall carry.' And so we find regarding the altar, that it was hollow inside, so that it would not be heavy." "<b>Pure.</b> Refined, without dross and without waste." "<b>A crown of gold around.</b> To cover its upper edge all around. For when one overlays it inside and out, the faces of its upper thickness were not yet overlaid, and the wood showed from there."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:21.584659455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}